(; constants used by Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Subgroup.Defs, declared with their translated types ;)

(; a constant applied as a function: DFunLike.coe ;)
AddSubgroupClass__inclusion__app : (a1 : Proof (Leq H K)) -> (a2 : Elem (Subtype G (x4 => Membership__mem G S H x4))) -> Elem (Subtype G (x5 => Membership__mem G S K x5)).

(; a constant applied as a function: DFunLike.coe ;)
AddSubgroupClass__subtype__app : (a1 : Elem S) -> (a2 : Elem (Subtype G (x3 => Membership__mem G S H x3))) -> Elem G.

(; a constant applied as a function: DFunLike.coe ;)
AddSubgroup__inclusion__app : (a1 : Proof (Leq H K)) -> (a2 : Elem (Subtype G (x3 => Membership__mem G (AddSubgroup G) H x3))) -> Elem (Subtype G (x4 => Membership__mem G (AddSubgroup G) K x4)).

(; a constant applied as a function: DFunLike.coe ;)
AddSubgroup__subtype__app : (a1 : Elem (AddSubgroup G)) -> (a2 : Elem (Subtype G (x2 => Membership__mem G (AddSubgroup G) s x2))) -> Elem G.

(; a constant applied as a function: DFunLike.coe ;)
SubgroupClass__inclusion__app : (a1 : Proof (Leq H K)) -> (a2 : Elem (Subtype G (x4 => Membership__mem G S H x4))) -> Elem (Subtype G (x5 => Membership__mem G S K x5)).

(; a constant applied as a function: DFunLike.coe ;)
SubgroupClass__subtype__app : (a1 : Elem S) -> (a2 : Elem (Subtype G (x3 => Membership__mem G S H x3))) -> Elem G.

(; a constant applied as a function: DFunLike.coe ;)
Subgroup__inclusion__app : (a1 : Proof (Leq H K)) -> (a2 : Elem (Subtype G (x3 => Membership__mem G (Subgroup G) H x3))) -> Elem (Subtype G (x4 => Membership__mem G (Subgroup G) K x4)).

(; a constant applied as a function: DFunLike.coe ;)
Subgroup__subtype__app : (a1 : Elem (Subgroup G)) -> (a2 : Elem (Subtype G (x2 => Membership__mem G (Subgroup G) s x2))) -> Elem G.

(; doc: An `AddGroup` is an `AddMonoid` with a unary `-` satisfying `-a + a = 0`.  There is also a binary operation `-` such that `a - b = a + -b`, with a default so that `a - b = a + -b` holds by definition.  Use `AddGroup.ofLeftAxioms` or `AddGroup.ofRightAxioms` to define an additive group structure on a type with the minimum proof obligations.  [Wikidata Q83478](https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q83478) ;)
(; //LEAN:AddGroup ;)
AddGroup : (A : Set) -> Prop.

(; doc: `AddMemClass S M` says `S` is a type of sets `s : Set M` that are closed under `(+)` ;)
(; //LEAN:AddMemClass ;)
AddMemClass : (S : Set) -> (M : Set) -> Prop.

(; doc: A substructure satisfying `AddMemClass` is closed under addition. ;)
(; //LEAN:AddMemClass.add_mem ;)
AddMemClass__add_mem : (S : Set) -> (M : Set) -> (x : Proof (Add M)) -> (x1 : Proof (SetLike S M)) -> (_ : Proof (AddMemClass S M)) -> (s : Elem S) -> (a : Elem M) -> (b : Elem M) -> (h : Proof (Membership__mem M S s a)) -> (h1 : Proof (Membership__mem M S s b)) -> Proof (Membership__mem M S s (plus a b)).

(; doc: `M →+ N` is the type of functions `M → N` that preserve the `AddZero` structure.  `AddMonoidHom` is also used for group homomorphisms.  When possible, instead of parametrizing results over `(f : M →+ N)`, you should parametrize over `(F : Type*) [AddMonoidHomClass F M N] (f : F)`.  When you extend this structure, make sure to extend `AddMonoidHomClass`.  [Wikidata Q868169](https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q868169) ;)
(; //LEAN:AddMonoidHom ;)
AddMonoidHom : (M : Set) -> (N : Set) -> Set.

(; doc: Composition of additive monoid morphisms as an additive monoid morphism. ;)
(; //LEAN:AddMonoidHom.comp ;)
AddMonoidHom__comp : (M : Set) -> (N : Set) -> (P : Set) -> (hnp : Elem (AddMonoidHom N P)) -> (hmn : Elem (AddMonoidHom M N)) -> Elem (AddMonoidHom M P).

(; //LEAN:AddMonoidHom.mk ;)
AddMonoidHom__mk : (M : Set) -> (N : Set) -> (toZeroHom : Elem (ZeroHom M N)) -> (map_add' : Proof (forall M (x2 => forall M (y => Eqt N (ZeroHom__toFun M N toZeroHom (plus x2 y)) (plus (ZeroHom__toFun M N toZeroHom x2) (ZeroHom__toFun M N toZeroHom y)))))) -> Elem (AddMonoidHom M N).

(; doc: Makes an additive group homomorphism from a proof that the map preserves addition. ;)
(; //LEAN:AddMonoidHom.mk' ;)
AddMonoidHom__mk' : (M : Set) -> (G : Set) -> (f : (Elem M -> G)) -> (map_add : Proof (forall M (a => forall M (b => Eqt G (f (plus a b)) (plus (f a) (f b)))))) -> Elem (AddMonoidHom M G).

(; //LEAN:AddSubgroup.copy._proof_1 ;)
AddSubgroup__copy___proof_1 : (G : Set) -> (_ : Proof (AddGroup G)) -> (K : Elem (AddSubgroup G)) -> (s : Elem (powerset G)) -> (hs : Proof (Eqt (powerset G) s (SetLike__coe (AddSubgroup G) G K))) -> (x1 : Elem G) -> (hx : Proof (Membership__mem G (powerset G) s x1)) -> Proof (Membership__mem G (powerset G) s (Neg__neg G x1)).

(; //LEAN:AddSubgroup.copy._proof_2 ;)
AddSubgroup__copy___proof_2 : (G : Set) -> (_ : Proof (AddGroup G)) -> (K : Elem (AddSubgroup G)) -> (s : Elem (powerset G)) -> (hs : Proof (Eqt (powerset G) s (SetLike__coe (AddSubgroup G) G K))) -> (x1 : Elem G) -> (x2 : Elem G) -> (h : Proof (Membership__mem G (powerset G) s x1)) -> (h1 : Proof (Membership__mem G (powerset G) s x2)) -> Proof (Membership__mem G (powerset G) s (plus x1 x2)).

(; //LEAN:AddSubgroup.copy._proof_3 ;)
AddSubgroup__copy___proof_3 : (G : Set) -> (_ : Proof (AddGroup G)) -> (K : Elem (AddSubgroup G)) -> (s : Elem (powerset G)) -> (hs : Proof (Eqt (powerset G) s (SetLike__coe (AddSubgroup G) G K))) -> Proof (Membership__mem G (powerset G) s 0).

(; //LEAN:AddSubgroup.inclusion._proof_1 ;)
AddSubgroup__inclusion___proof_1 : (G : Set) -> (_ : Proof (AddGroup G)) -> (H : Elem (AddSubgroup G)) -> (K : Elem (AddSubgroup G)) -> (h : Proof (Leq H K)) -> (x1 : Elem (Subtype G (x3 => Membership__mem G (AddSubgroup G) H x3))) -> Proof (Membership__mem G (AddSubgroup G) K (Subtype__val G (x2 => Membership__mem G (AddSubgroup G) H x2) x1)).

(; //LEAN:AddSubgroup.inclusion._proof_3 ;)
AddSubgroup__inclusion___proof_3 : (G : Set) -> (_ : Proof (AddGroup G)) -> (H : Elem (AddSubgroup G)) -> (K : Elem (AddSubgroup G)) -> (h : Proof (Leq H K)) -> (x1 : Elem (Subtype G (x9 => Membership__mem G (AddSubgroup G) H x9))) -> (x2 : Elem (Subtype G (x8 => Membership__mem G (AddSubgroup G) H x8))) -> Proof (Eqt (Subtype G (x3 => Membership__mem G (AddSubgroup G) K x3)) (Subtype__mk G (x4 => Membership__mem G (AddSubgroup G) K x4) (Subtype__val G (x5 => Membership__mem G (AddSubgroup G) H x5) (plus x1 x2)) (AddSubgroup__inclusion___proof_2 G H K h x1 x2)) (Subtype__mk G (x6 => Membership__mem G (AddSubgroup G) K x6) (Subtype__val G (x7 => Membership__mem G (AddSubgroup G) H x7) (plus x1 x2)) (AddSubgroup__inclusion___proof_2 G H K h x1 x2))).

(; //LEAN:AddSubgroup.instSetLike ;)
AddSubgroup__instSetLike : (G : Set) -> Proof (SetLike (AddSubgroup G) G).

(; //LEAN:AddSubgroup.normalizer._proof_1 ;)
AddSubgroup__normalizer___proof_1 : (G : Set) -> (_ : Proof (AddGroup G)) -> (S : Elem (powerset G)) -> (a : Elem G) -> (b : Elem G) -> (ha : Proof (forall G (n2 => iff (Membership__mem G (powerset G) S n2) (Membership__mem G (powerset G) S (plus (plus a n2) (Neg__neg G a)))))) -> (hb : Proof (forall G (n1 => iff (Membership__mem G (powerset G) S n1) (Membership__mem G (powerset G) S (plus (plus b n1) (Neg__neg G b)))))) -> (n : Elem G) -> Proof (iff (Membership__mem G (powerset G) S n) (Membership__mem G (powerset G) S (plus (plus (plus a b) n) (Neg__neg G (plus a b))))).

(; //LEAN:AddSubgroup.normalizer._proof_2 ;)
AddSubgroup__normalizer___proof_2 : (G : Set) -> (_ : Proof (AddGroup G)) -> (S : Elem (powerset G)) -> Proof (Membership__mem G (powerset G) (Set__ofPred G (g => forall G (n => iff (Membership__mem G (powerset G) S n) (Membership__mem G (powerset G) S (plus (plus g n) (Neg__neg G g)))))) 0).

(; //LEAN:AddSubgroup.normalizer._proof_3 ;)
AddSubgroup__normalizer___proof_3 : (G : Set) -> (_ : Proof (AddGroup G)) -> (S : Elem (powerset G)) -> (a : Elem G) -> (ha : Proof (forall G (n1 => iff (Membership__mem G (powerset G) S n1) (Membership__mem G (powerset G) S (plus (plus a n1) (Neg__neg G a)))))) -> (n : Elem G) -> Proof (iff (Membership__mem G (powerset G) S n) (Membership__mem G (powerset G) S (plus (plus (Neg__neg G a) n) (Neg__neg G (Neg__neg G a))))).

(; //LEAN:AddSubgroup.ofClass._proof_1 ;)
AddSubgroup__ofClass___proof_1 : (S : Set) -> (G : Set) -> (_ : Proof (AddGroup G)) -> (_ : Proof (AddSubgroupClass S G)) -> (s : Elem S) -> (x2 : Elem G) -> (x3 : Elem G) -> (h1 : Proof (Membership__mem G S s x2)) -> (h2 : Proof (Membership__mem G S s x3)) -> Proof (Membership__mem G S s (plus x2 x3)).

(; //LEAN:AddSubgroup.ofClass._proof_2 ;)
AddSubgroup__ofClass___proof_2 : (S : Set) -> (G : Set) -> (_ : Proof (AddGroup G)) -> (_ : Proof (AddSubgroupClass S G)) -> (s : Elem S) -> Proof (Membership__mem G S s 0).

(; //LEAN:AddSubgroup.ofClass._proof_3 ;)
AddSubgroup__ofClass___proof_3 : (S : Set) -> (G : Set) -> (_ : Proof (AddGroup G)) -> (_ : Proof (AddSubgroupClass S G)) -> (s : Elem S) -> (x2 : Elem G) -> (h1 : Proof (Membership__mem G S s x2)) -> Proof (Membership__mem G S s (Neg__neg G x2)).

(; //LEAN:AddSubgroup.ofSub._proof_3 ;)
AddSubgroup__ofSub___proof_3 : (G : Set) -> (_ : Proof (AddGroup G)) -> (s : Elem (powerset G)) -> (hsn : Proof (Set__Nonempty G s)) -> (hs : Proof (forall G (x1 => if (Membership__mem G (powerset G) s x1) (forall G (y => if (Membership__mem G (powerset G) s y) (Membership__mem G (powerset G) s (plus x1 (Neg__neg G y)))))))) -> Proof (Membership__mem G (powerset G) s 0).

(; //LEAN:AddSubgroup.ofSub._proof_4 ;)
AddSubgroup__ofSub___proof_4 : (G : Set) -> (_ : Proof (AddGroup G)) -> (s : Elem (powerset G)) -> (hs : Proof (forall G (x2 => if (Membership__mem G (powerset G) s x2) (forall G (y => if (Membership__mem G (powerset G) s y) (Membership__mem G (powerset G) s (plus x2 (Neg__neg G y)))))))) -> (zero_mem : Proof (Membership__mem G (powerset G) s 0)) -> (x1 : Elem G) -> (hx : Proof (Membership__mem G (powerset G) s x1)) -> Proof (Membership__mem G (powerset G) s (Neg__neg G x1)).

(; //LEAN:AddSubgroup.ofSub._proof_5 ;)
AddSubgroup__ofSub___proof_5 : (G : Set) -> (_ : Proof (AddGroup G)) -> (s : Elem (powerset G)) -> (hs : Proof (forall G (x4 => if (Membership__mem G (powerset G) s x4) (forall G (y => if (Membership__mem G (powerset G) s y) (Membership__mem G (powerset G) s (plus x4 (Neg__neg G y)))))))) -> (neg_mem : Proof (forall G (x3 => if (Membership__mem G (powerset G) s x3) (Membership__mem G (powerset G) s (Neg__neg G x3))))) -> (x1 : Elem G) -> (x2 : Elem G) -> (hx : Proof (Membership__mem G (powerset G) s x1)) -> (hy : Proof (Membership__mem G (powerset G) s x2)) -> Proof (Membership__mem G (powerset G) s (plus x1 x2)).

(; //LEAN:AddSubgroup.subtype._proof_2 ;)
AddSubgroup__subtype___proof_2 : (G : Set) -> (_ : Proof (AddGroup G)) -> (H : Elem (AddSubgroup G)) -> Proof (Eqt G (Subtype__val G (x1 => Membership__mem G (AddSubgroup G) H x1) 0) (Subtype__val G (x2 => Membership__mem G (AddSubgroup G) H x2) 0)).

(; //LEAN:AddSubgroup.subtype._proof_3 ;)
AddSubgroup__subtype___proof_3 : (G : Set) -> (_ : Proof (AddGroup G)) -> (H : Elem (AddSubgroup G)) -> (x1 : Elem (Subtype G (x6 => Membership__mem G (AddSubgroup G) H x6))) -> (x2 : Elem (Subtype G (x5 => Membership__mem G (AddSubgroup G) H x5))) -> Proof (Eqt G (Subtype__val G (x3 => Membership__mem G (AddSubgroup G) H x3) (plus x1 x2)) (Subtype__val G (x4 => Membership__mem G (AddSubgroup G) H x4) (plus x1 x2))).

(; //LEAN:AddSubgroupClass.inclusion._proof_1 ;)
AddSubgroupClass__inclusion___proof_1 : (G : Set) -> (S : Set) -> (_ : Proof (LE S)) -> (_ : Proof (IsConcreteLE S G)) -> (H : Elem S) -> (K : Elem S) -> (h1 : Proof (Leq H K)) -> (x2 : Elem (Subtype G (x4 => Membership__mem G S H x4))) -> Proof (Membership__mem G S K (Subtype__val G (x3 => Membership__mem G S H x3) x2)).

(; //LEAN:AddSubgroupClass.inclusion._proof_3 ;)
AddSubgroupClass__inclusion___proof_3 : (G : Set) -> (_ : Proof (AddGroup G)) -> (S : Set) -> (_ : Proof (AddSubgroupClass S G)) -> (_ : Proof (LE S)) -> (_ : Proof (IsConcreteLE S G)) -> (H : Elem S) -> (K : Elem S) -> (h2 : Proof (Leq H K)) -> (x3 : Elem (Subtype G (x11 => Membership__mem G S H x11))) -> (x4 : Elem (Subtype G (x10 => Membership__mem G S H x10))) -> Proof (Eqt (Subtype G (x5 => Membership__mem G S K x5)) (Subtype__mk G (x6 => Membership__mem G S K x6) (Subtype__val G (x7 => Membership__mem G S H x7) (plus x3 x4)) (AddSubgroupClass__inclusion___proof_2 G S H K h2 x3 x4)) (Subtype__mk G (x8 => Membership__mem G S K x8) (Subtype__val G (x9 => Membership__mem G S H x9) (plus x3 x4)) (AddSubgroupClass__inclusion___proof_2 G S H K h2 x3 x4))).

(; //LEAN:AddSubgroupClass.subtype._proof_1 ;)
AddSubgroupClass__subtype___proof_1 : (G : Set) -> (_ : Proof (AddGroup G)) -> (S : Set) -> (H : Elem S) -> (_ : Proof (AddSubgroupClass S G)) -> Proof (Eqt G (Subtype__val G (x2 => Membership__mem G S H x2) 0) (Subtype__val G (x3 => Membership__mem G S H x3) 0)).

(; //LEAN:AddSubgroupClass.subtype._proof_2 ;)
AddSubgroupClass__subtype___proof_2 : (G : Set) -> (_ : Proof (AddGroup G)) -> (S : Set) -> (H : Elem S) -> (_ : Proof (AddSubgroupClass S G)) -> (x2 : Elem (Subtype G (x7 => Membership__mem G S H x7))) -> (x3 : Elem (Subtype G (x6 => Membership__mem G S H x6))) -> Proof (Eqt G (Subtype__val G (x4 => Membership__mem G S H x4) (plus x2 x3)) (Subtype__val G (x5 => Membership__mem G S H x5) (plus x2 x3))).

(; doc: An additive submonoid of an additive monoid `M` is a subset containing 0 and closed under addition. ;)
(; //LEAN:AddSubmonoid ;)
AddSubmonoid : (M : Set) -> Set.

(; //LEAN:AddSubmonoid.mk ;)
AddSubmonoid__mk : (M : Set) -> (toAddSubsemigroup : Elem (AddSubsemigroup M)) -> (zero_mem' : Proof (Membership__mem M (powerset M) (AddSubsemigroup__carrier M toAddSubsemigroup) 0)) -> Elem (AddSubmonoid M).

(; //LEAN:AddSubmonoid.mk_eq_zero ;)
AddSubmonoid__mk_eq_zero : (M : Set) -> (_ : Proof (AddZeroClass M)) -> (S : Elem (AddSubmonoid M)) -> (a : Elem M) -> (ha : Proof (Membership__mem M (AddSubmonoid M) S a)) -> Proof (iff (Eqt (Subtype M (x1 => Membership__mem M (AddSubmonoid M) S x1)) (Subtype__mk M (x2 => Membership__mem M (AddSubmonoid M) S x2) a ha) 0) (Eqt M a 0)).

(; doc: An additive submonoid of an additive monoid `M` can be considered as an additive subsemigroup of that additive monoid. ;)
(; //LEAN:AddSubmonoid.toAddSubsemigroup ;)
AddSubmonoid__toAddSubsemigroup : (M : Set) -> (self : Elem (AddSubmonoid M)) -> Elem (AddSubsemigroup M).

(; doc: `AddSubmonoidClass S M` says `S` is a type of subsets `s ≤ M` that contain `0` and are closed under `(+)` ;)
(; //LEAN:AddSubmonoidClass ;)
AddSubmonoidClass : (S : Set) -> (M : Set) -> Prop.

(; doc: The carrier of an additive subsemigroup. ;)
(; //LEAN:AddSubsemigroup.carrier ;)
AddSubsemigroup__carrier : (M : Set) -> (self : Elem (AddSubsemigroup M)) -> Elem (powerset M).

(; //LEAN:AddSubsemigroup.mk ;)
AddSubsemigroup__mk : (M : Set) -> (carrier : Elem (powerset M)) -> (add_mem' : Proof (forall M (a => forall M (b => if (Membership__mem M (powerset M) carrier a) (if (Membership__mem M (powerset M) carrier b) (Membership__mem M (powerset M) carrier (plus a b))))))) -> Elem (AddSubsemigroup M).

(; //LEAN:AddZero.toAdd ;)
AddZero__toAdd : (M : Set) -> Proof (Add M).

(; doc: A `DivInvMonoid` is a `Monoid` with operations `/` and `⁻¹` satisfying `div_eq_mul_inv : ∀ a b, a / b = a * b⁻¹`.  This deduplicates the name `div_eq_mul_inv`. The default for `div` is such that `a / b = a * b⁻¹` holds by definition.  Adding `div` as a field rather than defining `a / b := a * b⁻¹` allows us to avoid certain classes of unification failures, for example: Let `Foo X` be a type with a `∀ X, Div (Foo X)` instance but no `∀ X, Inv (Foo X)`, e.g. when `Foo X` is a `EuclideanDomain`. Suppose we also have an instance `∀ X [Cromulent X], GroupWithZero (Foo X)`. Then the `(/)` coming from `GroupWithZero.div` cannot be definitionally equal to the `(/)` coming from `Foo.Div`.  In the same way, adding a `zpow` field makes it possible to avoid definitional failures in diamonds. See the definition of `Monoid` and Note [forgetful inheritance] for more explanations on this. ;)
(; //LEAN:DivInvMonoid ;)
DivInvMonoid : (G : Set) -> Prop.

(; //LEAN:DivInvMonoid.toInv ;)
DivInvMonoid__toInv : (G : Set) -> Proof (Inv G).

(; doc: Equality is symmetric: if `a = b` then `b = a`.  Because this is in the `Eq` namespace, if you have a variable `h : a = b`, `h.symm` can be used as shorthand for `Eq.symm h` as a proof of `b = a`.  For more information: [Equality](https://lean-lang.org/theorem_proving_in_lean4/quantifiers_and_equality.html#equality) ;)
(; //LEAN:Eq.symm ;)
Eq__symm : (X : Set) -> (a : Elem X) -> (b : Elem X) -> (h : Proof (Eqt X a b)) -> Proof (Eqt X b a).

(; doc: A function `f : α → β` is called injective if `f x = f y` implies `x = y`. ;)
(; //LEAN:Function.Injective ;)
Function__Injective : (X : Set) -> (Y : Set) -> (f : (Elem X -> Y)) -> Prop.

(; //LEAN:Function.Injective.eq_iff ;)
Function__Injective__eq_iff : (X : Set) -> (Y : Set) -> (f : (Elem X -> Y)) -> (I : Proof (Function__Injective X Y f)) -> (a : Elem X) -> (b : Elem X) -> Proof (iff (Eqt Y (f a) (f b)) (Eqt X a b)).

(; doc: A `Group` is a `Monoid` with an operation `⁻¹` satisfying `a⁻¹ * a = 1`.  There is also a division operation `/` such that `a / b = a * b⁻¹`, with a default so that `a / b = a * b⁻¹` holds by definition.  Use `Group.ofLeftAxioms` or `Group.ofRightAxioms` to define a group structure on a type with the minimum proof obligations.  [Wikidata Q83478](https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q83478) ;)
(; //LEAN:Group ;)
Group : (G : Set) -> Prop.

(; doc: `a • b` computes the product of `a` and `b`. The meaning of this notation is type-dependent, but it is intended to be used for left actions.  Conventions for notations in identifiers:   * The recommended spelling of `•` in identifiers is `smul`. ;)
(; //LEAN:HSMul.hSMul ;)
HSMul__hSMul : (X : Set) -> (Y : Set) -> (Z : Set) -> (x : Elem X) -> (x1 : Elem Y) -> Elem Z.

(; //LEAN:Iff.rfl ;)
Iff__rfl : (a : Prop) -> Proof (iff a a).

(; doc: The notation typeclass for inverses. This enables the notation `a⁻¹ : α` where `a : α`. ;)
(; //LEAN:Inv ;)
Inv : (X : Set) -> Prop.

(; doc: `a⁻¹` computes the inverse of `a`. The meaning of this notation is type-dependent.  Conventions for notations in identifiers:   * The recommended spelling of `⁻¹` in identifiers is `inv`. ;)
(; //LEAN:Inv.inv ;)
Inv__inv : (X : Set) -> (x : Elem X) -> Elem X.

(; //LEAN:InvOneClass.toInv ;)
InvOneClass__toInv : (G : Set) -> Proof (Inv G).

(; //LEAN:InvOneClass.toOne ;)
InvOneClass__toOne : (G : Set) -> Proof (One G).

(; doc: Auxiliary typeclass for types with an involutive `Inv`. ;)
(; //LEAN:InvolutiveInv ;)
InvolutiveInv : (G : Set) -> Prop.

(; doc: Auxiliary typeclass for types with an involutive `Neg`. ;)
(; //LEAN:InvolutiveNeg ;)
InvolutiveNeg : (A : Set) -> Prop.

(; doc: A class to indicate that the order on a type corresponds to set inclusion.  An instance of this class is automatically available on any order defined via `LE.ofMembership`. ;)
(; //LEAN:IsConcreteLE ;)
IsConcreteLE : (A : Set) -> (B : Set) -> Prop.

(; doc: `LE α` is the typeclass which supports the notation `x ≤ y` where `x y : α`. ;)
(; //LEAN:LE ;)
LE : (X : Set) -> Prop.

(; doc: **Alias** of `le_trans`. ;)
(; //LEAN:LE.le.trans ;)
LE__le__trans : (X : Set) -> (_ : Proof (Preorder X)) -> (a : Elem X) -> (b : Elem X) -> (c : Elem X) -> (h : Proof (Leq a b)) -> (h1 : Proof (Leq b c)) -> Proof (Leq a c).

(; doc: The membership relation `a ∈ s : Prop` where `a : α`, `s : γ`.  Conventions for notations in identifiers:   * The recommended spelling of `∈` in identifiers is `mem`. ;)
(; //LEAN:Membership.mem ;)
Membership__mem : (X : Set) -> (Z : Set) -> (x : Elem Z) -> (x1 : Elem X) -> Prop.

(; doc: `M →* N` is the type of functions `M → N` that preserve the `MulOne` structure. `MonoidHom` is used for both monoid and group homomorphisms.  When possible, instead of parametrizing results over `(f : M →* N)`, you should parametrize over `(F : Type*) [MonoidHomClass F M N] (f : F)`.  When you extend this structure, make sure to extend `MonoidHomClass`.  [Wikidata Q868169](https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q868169) ;)
(; //LEAN:MonoidHom ;)
MonoidHom : (M : Set) -> (N : Set) -> Set.

(; doc: Composition of monoid morphisms as a monoid morphism. ;)
(; //LEAN:MonoidHom.comp ;)
MonoidHom__comp : (M : Set) -> (N : Set) -> (P : Set) -> (hnp : Elem (MonoidHom N P)) -> (hmn : Elem (MonoidHom M N)) -> Elem (MonoidHom M P).

(; //LEAN:MonoidHom.mk ;)
MonoidHom__mk : (M : Set) -> (N : Set) -> (toOneHom : Elem (OneHom M N)) -> (map_mul' : Proof (forall M (x2 => forall M (y => Eqt N (OneHom__toFun M N toOneHom (times x2 y)) (times (OneHom__toFun M N toOneHom x2) (OneHom__toFun M N toOneHom y)))))) -> Elem (MonoidHom M N).

(; doc: Makes a group homomorphism from a proof that the map preserves multiplication. ;)
(; //LEAN:MonoidHom.mk' ;)
MonoidHom__mk' : (M : Set) -> (G : Set) -> (f : (Elem M -> G)) -> (map_mul : Proof (forall M (a => forall M (b => Eqt G (f (times a b)) (times (f a) (f b)))))) -> Elem (MonoidHom M G).

(; doc: A function `f` is monotone if `a ≤ b` implies `f a ≤ f b`. ;)
(; //LEAN:Monotone ;)
Monotone : (X : Set) -> (Y : Set) -> (f : (Elem X -> Y)) -> Prop.

(; doc: `MulMemClass S M` says `S` is a type of sets `s : Set M` that are closed under `(*)` ;)
(; //LEAN:MulMemClass ;)
MulMemClass : (S : Set) -> (M : Set) -> Prop.

(; doc: A substructure satisfying `MulMemClass` is closed under multiplication. ;)
(; //LEAN:MulMemClass.mul_mem ;)
MulMemClass__mul_mem : (S : Set) -> (M : Set) -> (x : Proof (Mul M)) -> (x1 : Proof (SetLike S M)) -> (_ : Proof (MulMemClass S M)) -> (s : Elem S) -> (a : Elem M) -> (b : Elem M) -> (h : Proof (Membership__mem M S s a)) -> (h1 : Proof (Membership__mem M S s b)) -> Proof (Membership__mem M S s (times a b)).

(; //LEAN:MulOne.toMul ;)
MulOne__toMul : (M : Set) -> Proof (Mul M).

(; doc: The notation typeclass for negation. This enables the notation `-a : α` where `a : α`. ;)
(; //LEAN:Neg ;)
Neg : (X : Set) -> Prop.

(; doc: `-a` computes the negative or opposite of `a`. The meaning of this notation is type-dependent.  Conventions for notations in identifiers:   * The recommended spelling of `-` in identifiers is `neg` (when used as a unary operator). ;)
(; //LEAN:Neg.neg ;)
Neg__neg : (X : Set) -> (x : Elem X) -> Elem X.

(; //LEAN:NegZeroClass.toNeg ;)
NegZeroClass__toNeg : (G : Set) -> Proof (Neg G).

(; //LEAN:NegZeroClass.toZero ;)
NegZeroClass__toZero : (G : Set) -> Proof (Zero G).

(; //LEAN:OneHom.mk ;)
OneHom__mk : (M : Set) -> (N : Set) -> (toFun : (Elem M -> N)) -> (map_one' : Proof (Eqt N (toFun 1) 1)) -> Elem (OneHom M N).

(; doc: `OneMemClass S M` says `S` is a type of subsets `s ≤ M`, such that `1 ∈ s` for all `s`. ;)
(; //LEAN:OneMemClass ;)
OneMemClass : (S : Set) -> (M : Set) -> Prop.

(; doc: By definition, if we have `OneMemClass S M`, we have `1 ∈ s` for all `s : S`. ;)
(; //LEAN:OneMemClass.one_mem ;)
OneMemClass__one_mem : (S : Set) -> (M : Set) -> (x : Proof (One M)) -> (x1 : Proof (SetLike S M)) -> (_ : Proof (OneMemClass S M)) -> (s : Elem S) -> Proof (Membership__mem M S s 1).

(; doc: A preorder is a reflexive, transitive relation `≤`. In a preorder, `a < b` means `a ≤ b ∧ ¬b ≤ a`, and `<` is defined this way by default. You can override this definition to set a better def-eq. ;)
(; //LEAN:Preorder ;)
Preorder : (X : Set) -> Prop.

(; doc: `f` is injective on `s` if the restriction of `f` to `s` is injective. ;)
(; //LEAN:Set.InjOn ;)
Set__InjOn : (X : Set) -> (Y : Set) -> (f : (Elem X -> Y)) -> (s : Elem (powerset X)) -> Prop.

(; doc: The property `s.Nonempty` expresses the fact that the set `s` is not empty. It should be used in theorem assumptions instead of `∃ x, x ∈ s` or `s ≠ ∅` as it gives access to a nice API thanks to the dot notation. ;)
(; //LEAN:Set.Nonempty ;)
Set__Nonempty : (X : Set) -> (s : Elem (powerset X)) -> Prop.

(; doc: The subset relation on sets. `s ⊆ t` means that all elements of `s` are elements of `t`.  Note that you should **not** use this definition directly, but instead write `s ⊆ t`. ;)
(; //LEAN:Set.Subset ;)
Set__Subset : (X : Set) -> (s1 : Elem (powerset X)) -> (s2 : Elem (powerset X)) -> Prop.

(; //LEAN:Set.coe_inclusion ;)
Set__coe_inclusion : (X : Set) -> (s : Elem (powerset X)) -> (t : Elem (powerset X)) -> (h : Proof (Set__Subset X s t)) -> (x : Elem (Set__Elem X s)) -> Proof (Eqt X (Subtype__val X (x1 => Membership__mem X (powerset X) t x1) (Set__inclusion X s t h x)) (Subtype__val X (x2 => Membership__mem X (powerset X) s x2) x)).

(; //LEAN:Set.inclusion_injective ;)
Set__inclusion_injective : (X : Set) -> (s : Elem (powerset X)) -> (t : Elem (powerset X)) -> (h : Proof (Set__Subset X s t)) -> Proof (Function__Injective (Set__Elem X s) (Set__Elem X t) (Set__inclusion X s t h)).

(; doc: Turn a predicate `p : α → Prop` into a set, also written as `{x | p x}` ;)
(; //LEAN:Set.ofPred ;)
Set__ofPred : (X : Set) -> (Mem : (Elem X -> Prop)) -> Elem (powerset X).

(; doc: A class to indicate that there is a canonical injection between `A` and `Set B`.  This has the effect of giving terms of `A` elements of type `B` (through a `Membership` instance) and a compatible coercion to `Type*` as a subtype.  Note: if `SetLike.coe` is a projection, implementers should create a simp lemma such as ``` @[simp] lemma mem_carrier {p : MySubobject X} : x ∈ p.carrier ↔ x ∈ (p : Set X) := Iff.rfl ``` to normalize terms.  If you declare an unbundled subclass of `SetLike`, for example: ``` class MulMemClass (S : Type*) (M : Type*) [Mul M] [SetLike S M] where   ... ``` Then you should *not* repeat the `outParam` declaration so `SetLike` will supply the value instead. This ensures your subclass will not have issues with synthesis of the `[Mul M]` parameter starting before the value of `M` is known. ;)
(; //LEAN:SetLike ;)
SetLike : (A : Set) -> (B : Set) -> Prop.

(; doc: The coercion from a term of a `SetLike` to its corresponding `Set`. ;)
(; //LEAN:SetLike.coe ;)
SetLike__coe : (A : Set) -> (B : Set) -> (x : Elem A) -> Elem (powerset B).

(; doc: The coercion from a term of a `SetLike` to its corresponding `Set` is injective. ;)
(; //LEAN:SetLike.coe_injective ;)
SetLike__coe_injective : (A : Set) -> (B : Set) -> Proof (Function__Injective A (powerset B) (SetLike__coe A B)).

(; //LEAN:SetLike.coe_subset_coe ;)
SetLike__coe_subset_coe : (A : Set) -> (B : Set) -> (_ : Proof (LE A)) -> (_ : Proof (IsConcreteLE A B)) -> (p : Elem A) -> (q : Elem A) -> Proof (iff (Set__Subset B (SetLike__coe A B p) (SetLike__coe A B q)) (Leq p q)).

(; doc: Note: implementers of `SetLike` must copy this lemma in order to tag it with `@[ext]`. ;)
(; //LEAN:SetLike.ext ;)
SetLike__ext : (A : Set) -> (B : Set) -> (p : Elem A) -> (q : Elem A) -> (h : Proof (forall B (x => iff (Membership__mem B A p x) (Membership__mem B A q x)))) -> Proof (Eqt A p q).

(; //LEAN:SetLike.ext'_iff ;)
SetLike__ext'_iff : (A : Set) -> (B : Set) -> (p : Elem A) -> (q : Elem A) -> Proof (iff (Eqt A p q) (Eqt (powerset B) (SetLike__coe A B p) (SetLike__coe A B q))).

(; //LEAN:SetLike.instMembership ;)
SetLike__instMembership : (A : Set) -> (B : Set) -> Proof (Membership B A).

(; //LEAN:SetLike.mem_coe ;)
SetLike__mem_coe : (A : Set) -> (B : Set) -> (p : Elem A) -> (x : Elem B) -> Proof (iff (Membership__mem B (powerset B) (SetLike__coe A B p) x) (Membership__mem B A p x)).

(; doc: A function `f` is strictly monotone if `a < b` implies `f a < f b`. ;)
(; //LEAN:StrictMono ;)
StrictMono : (X : Set) -> (Y : Set) -> (f : (Elem X -> Y)) -> Prop.

(; //LEAN:StrictMono.monotone ;)
StrictMono__monotone : (X : Set) -> (Y : Set) -> (_ : Proof (PartialOrder X)) -> (_ : Proof (Preorder Y)) -> (f : (Elem X -> Y)) -> (hf : Proof (StrictMono X Y f)) -> Proof (Monotone X Y f).

(; doc: A `SubNegMonoid` is an `AddMonoid` with unary `-` and binary `-` operations satisfying `sub_eq_add_neg : ∀ a b, a - b = a + -b`.  The default for `sub` is such that `a - b = a + -b` holds by definition.  Adding `sub` as a field rather than defining `a - b := a + -b` allows us to avoid certain classes of unification failures, for example: Let `foo X` be a type with a `∀ X, Sub (Foo X)` instance but no `∀ X, Neg (Foo X)`. Suppose we also have an instance `∀ X [Cromulent X], AddGroup (Foo X)`. Then the `(-)` coming from `AddGroup.sub` cannot be definitionally equal to the `(-)` coming from `Foo.Sub`.  In the same way, adding a `zsmul` field makes it possible to avoid definitional failures in diamonds. See the definition of `AddMonoid` and Note [forgetful inheritance] for more explanations on this. ;)
(; //LEAN:SubNegMonoid ;)
SubNegMonoid : (G : Set) -> Prop.

(; //LEAN:SubNegMonoid.toNeg ;)
SubNegMonoid__toNeg : (G : Set) -> Proof (Neg G).

(; //LEAN:Subgroup.copy._proof_1 ;)
Subgroup__copy___proof_1 : (G : Set) -> (_ : Proof (Group G)) -> (K : Elem (Subgroup G)) -> (s : Elem (powerset G)) -> (hs : Proof (Eqt (powerset G) s (SetLike__coe (Subgroup G) G K))) -> (x1 : Elem G) -> (hx : Proof (Membership__mem G (powerset G) s x1)) -> Proof (Membership__mem G (powerset G) s (Inv__inv G x1)).

(; //LEAN:Subgroup.copy._proof_2 ;)
Subgroup__copy___proof_2 : (G : Set) -> (_ : Proof (Group G)) -> (K : Elem (Subgroup G)) -> (s : Elem (powerset G)) -> (hs : Proof (Eqt (powerset G) s (SetLike__coe (Subgroup G) G K))) -> (x1 : Elem G) -> (x2 : Elem G) -> (h : Proof (Membership__mem G (powerset G) s x1)) -> (h1 : Proof (Membership__mem G (powerset G) s x2)) -> Proof (Membership__mem G (powerset G) s (times x1 x2)).

(; //LEAN:Subgroup.copy._proof_3 ;)
Subgroup__copy___proof_3 : (G : Set) -> (_ : Proof (Group G)) -> (K : Elem (Subgroup G)) -> (s : Elem (powerset G)) -> (hs : Proof (Eqt (powerset G) s (SetLike__coe (Subgroup G) G K))) -> Proof (Membership__mem G (powerset G) s 1).

(; //LEAN:Subgroup.inclusion._proof_1 ;)
Subgroup__inclusion___proof_1 : (G : Set) -> (_ : Proof (Group G)) -> (H : Elem (Subgroup G)) -> (K : Elem (Subgroup G)) -> (h : Proof (Leq H K)) -> (x1 : Elem (Subtype G (x3 => Membership__mem G (Subgroup G) H x3))) -> Proof (Membership__mem G (Subgroup G) K (Subtype__val G (x2 => Membership__mem G (Subgroup G) H x2) x1)).

(; //LEAN:Subgroup.inclusion._proof_3 ;)
Subgroup__inclusion___proof_3 : (G : Set) -> (_ : Proof (Group G)) -> (H : Elem (Subgroup G)) -> (K : Elem (Subgroup G)) -> (h : Proof (Leq H K)) -> (x1 : Elem (Subtype G (x9 => Membership__mem G (Subgroup G) H x9))) -> (x2 : Elem (Subtype G (x8 => Membership__mem G (Subgroup G) H x8))) -> Proof (Eqt (Subtype G (x3 => Membership__mem G (Subgroup G) K x3)) (Subtype__mk G (x4 => Membership__mem G (Subgroup G) K x4) (Subtype__val G (x5 => Membership__mem G (Subgroup G) H x5) (times x1 x2)) (Subgroup__inclusion___proof_2 G H K h x1 x2)) (Subtype__mk G (x6 => Membership__mem G (Subgroup G) K x6) (Subtype__val G (x7 => Membership__mem G (Subgroup G) H x7) (times x1 x2)) (Subgroup__inclusion___proof_2 G H K h x1 x2))).

(; //LEAN:Subgroup.instSetLike ;)
Subgroup__instSetLike : (G : Set) -> Proof (SetLike (Subgroup G) G).

(; //LEAN:Subgroup.normalizer._proof_1 ;)
Subgroup__normalizer___proof_1 : (G : Set) -> (_ : Proof (Group G)) -> (S : Elem (powerset G)) -> (a : Elem G) -> (b : Elem G) -> (ha : Proof (forall G (n2 => iff (Membership__mem G (powerset G) S n2) (Membership__mem G (powerset G) S (times (times a n2) (Inv__inv G a)))))) -> (hb : Proof (forall G (n1 => iff (Membership__mem G (powerset G) S n1) (Membership__mem G (powerset G) S (times (times b n1) (Inv__inv G b)))))) -> (n : Elem G) -> Proof (iff (Membership__mem G (powerset G) S n) (Membership__mem G (powerset G) S (times (times (times a b) n) (Inv__inv G (times a b))))).

(; //LEAN:Subgroup.normalizer._proof_2 ;)
Subgroup__normalizer___proof_2 : (G : Set) -> (_ : Proof (Group G)) -> (S : Elem (powerset G)) -> Proof (Membership__mem G (powerset G) (Set__ofPred G (g => forall G (n => iff (Membership__mem G (powerset G) S n) (Membership__mem G (powerset G) S (times (times g n) (Inv__inv G g)))))) 1).

(; //LEAN:Subgroup.normalizer._proof_3 ;)
Subgroup__normalizer___proof_3 : (G : Set) -> (_ : Proof (Group G)) -> (S : Elem (powerset G)) -> (a : Elem G) -> (ha : Proof (forall G (n1 => iff (Membership__mem G (powerset G) S n1) (Membership__mem G (powerset G) S (times (times a n1) (Inv__inv G a)))))) -> (n : Elem G) -> Proof (iff (Membership__mem G (powerset G) S n) (Membership__mem G (powerset G) S (times (times (Inv__inv G a) n) (Inv__inv G (Inv__inv G a))))).

(; //LEAN:Subgroup.ofClass._proof_1 ;)
Subgroup__ofClass___proof_1 : (S : Set) -> (G : Set) -> (_ : Proof (Group G)) -> (_ : Proof (SubgroupClass S G)) -> (s : Elem S) -> (x2 : Elem G) -> (x3 : Elem G) -> (h1 : Proof (Membership__mem G S s x2)) -> (h2 : Proof (Membership__mem G S s x3)) -> Proof (Membership__mem G S s (times x2 x3)).

(; //LEAN:Subgroup.ofClass._proof_2 ;)
Subgroup__ofClass___proof_2 : (S : Set) -> (G : Set) -> (_ : Proof (Group G)) -> (_ : Proof (SubgroupClass S G)) -> (s : Elem S) -> Proof (Membership__mem G S s 1).

(; //LEAN:Subgroup.ofClass._proof_3 ;)
Subgroup__ofClass___proof_3 : (S : Set) -> (G : Set) -> (_ : Proof (Group G)) -> (_ : Proof (SubgroupClass S G)) -> (s : Elem S) -> (x2 : Elem G) -> (h1 : Proof (Membership__mem G S s x2)) -> Proof (Membership__mem G S s (Inv__inv G x2)).

(; //LEAN:Subgroup.ofDiv._proof_3 ;)
Subgroup__ofDiv___proof_3 : (G : Set) -> (_ : Proof (Group G)) -> (s : Elem (powerset G)) -> (hsn : Proof (Set__Nonempty G s)) -> (hs : Proof (forall G (x1 => if (Membership__mem G (powerset G) s x1) (forall G (y => if (Membership__mem G (powerset G) s y) (Membership__mem G (powerset G) s (times x1 (Inv__inv G y)))))))) -> Proof (Membership__mem G (powerset G) s 1).

(; //LEAN:Subgroup.ofDiv._proof_4 ;)
Subgroup__ofDiv___proof_4 : (G : Set) -> (_ : Proof (Group G)) -> (s : Elem (powerset G)) -> (hs : Proof (forall G (x2 => if (Membership__mem G (powerset G) s x2) (forall G (y => if (Membership__mem G (powerset G) s y) (Membership__mem G (powerset G) s (times x2 (Inv__inv G y)))))))) -> (one_mem : Proof (Membership__mem G (powerset G) s 1)) -> (x1 : Elem G) -> (hx : Proof (Membership__mem G (powerset G) s x1)) -> Proof (Membership__mem G (powerset G) s (Inv__inv G x1)).

(; //LEAN:Subgroup.ofDiv._proof_5 ;)
Subgroup__ofDiv___proof_5 : (G : Set) -> (_ : Proof (Group G)) -> (s : Elem (powerset G)) -> (hs : Proof (forall G (x4 => if (Membership__mem G (powerset G) s x4) (forall G (y => if (Membership__mem G (powerset G) s y) (Membership__mem G (powerset G) s (times x4 (Inv__inv G y)))))))) -> (inv_mem : Proof (forall G (x3 => if (Membership__mem G (powerset G) s x3) (Membership__mem G (powerset G) s (Inv__inv G x3))))) -> (x1 : Elem G) -> (x2 : Elem G) -> (hx : Proof (Membership__mem G (powerset G) s x1)) -> (hy : Proof (Membership__mem G (powerset G) s x2)) -> Proof (Membership__mem G (powerset G) s (times x1 x2)).

(; //LEAN:Subgroup.subtype._proof_2 ;)
Subgroup__subtype___proof_2 : (G : Set) -> (_ : Proof (Group G)) -> (H : Elem (Subgroup G)) -> Proof (Eqt G (Subtype__val G (x1 => Membership__mem G (Subgroup G) H x1) 1) (Subtype__val G (x2 => Membership__mem G (Subgroup G) H x2) 1)).

(; //LEAN:Subgroup.subtype._proof_3 ;)
Subgroup__subtype___proof_3 : (G : Set) -> (_ : Proof (Group G)) -> (H : Elem (Subgroup G)) -> (x1 : Elem (Subtype G (x6 => Membership__mem G (Subgroup G) H x6))) -> (x2 : Elem (Subtype G (x5 => Membership__mem G (Subgroup G) H x5))) -> Proof (Eqt G (Subtype__val G (x3 => Membership__mem G (Subgroup G) H x3) (times x1 x2)) (Subtype__val G (x4 => Membership__mem G (Subgroup G) H x4) (times x1 x2))).

(; //LEAN:SubgroupClass.inclusion._proof_1 ;)
SubgroupClass__inclusion___proof_1 : (G : Set) -> (S : Set) -> (_ : Proof (LE S)) -> (_ : Proof (IsConcreteLE S G)) -> (H : Elem S) -> (K : Elem S) -> (h1 : Proof (Leq H K)) -> (x2 : Elem (Subtype G (x4 => Membership__mem G S H x4))) -> Proof (Membership__mem G S K (Subtype__val G (x3 => Membership__mem G S H x3) x2)).

(; //LEAN:SubgroupClass.inclusion._proof_3 ;)
SubgroupClass__inclusion___proof_3 : (G : Set) -> (_ : Proof (Group G)) -> (S : Set) -> (_ : Proof (SubgroupClass S G)) -> (_ : Proof (LE S)) -> (_ : Proof (IsConcreteLE S G)) -> (H : Elem S) -> (K : Elem S) -> (h2 : Proof (Leq H K)) -> (x3 : Elem (Subtype G (x11 => Membership__mem G S H x11))) -> (x4 : Elem (Subtype G (x10 => Membership__mem G S H x10))) -> Proof (Eqt (Subtype G (x5 => Membership__mem G S K x5)) (Subtype__mk G (x6 => Membership__mem G S K x6) (Subtype__val G (x7 => Membership__mem G S H x7) (times x3 x4)) (SubgroupClass__inclusion___proof_2 G S H K h2 x3 x4)) (Subtype__mk G (x8 => Membership__mem G S K x8) (Subtype__val G (x9 => Membership__mem G S H x9) (times x3 x4)) (SubgroupClass__inclusion___proof_2 G S H K h2 x3 x4))).

(; //LEAN:SubgroupClass.subtype._proof_1 ;)
SubgroupClass__subtype___proof_1 : (G : Set) -> (_ : Proof (Group G)) -> (S : Set) -> (H : Elem S) -> (_ : Proof (SubgroupClass S G)) -> Proof (Eqt G (Subtype__val G (x2 => Membership__mem G S H x2) 1) (Subtype__val G (x3 => Membership__mem G S H x3) 1)).

(; //LEAN:SubgroupClass.subtype._proof_2 ;)
SubgroupClass__subtype___proof_2 : (G : Set) -> (_ : Proof (Group G)) -> (S : Set) -> (H : Elem S) -> (_ : Proof (SubgroupClass S G)) -> (x2 : Elem (Subtype G (x7 => Membership__mem G S H x7))) -> (x3 : Elem (Subtype G (x6 => Membership__mem G S H x6))) -> Proof (Eqt G (Subtype__val G (x4 => Membership__mem G S H x4) (times x2 x3)) (Subtype__val G (x5 => Membership__mem G S H x5) (times x2 x3))).

(; doc: A submonoid of a monoid `M` is a subset containing 1 and closed under multiplication. ;)
(; //LEAN:Submonoid ;)
Submonoid : (M : Set) -> Set.

(; //LEAN:Submonoid.mk ;)
Submonoid__mk : (M : Set) -> (toSubsemigroup : Elem (Subsemigroup M)) -> (one_mem' : Proof (Membership__mem M (powerset M) (Subsemigroup__carrier M toSubsemigroup) 1)) -> Elem (Submonoid M).

(; //LEAN:Submonoid.mk_eq_one ;)
Submonoid__mk_eq_one : (M : Set) -> (_ : Proof (MulOneClass M)) -> (S : Elem (Submonoid M)) -> (a : Elem M) -> (ha : Proof (Membership__mem M (Submonoid M) S a)) -> Proof (iff (Eqt (Subtype M (x1 => Membership__mem M (Submonoid M) S x1)) (Subtype__mk M (x2 => Membership__mem M (Submonoid M) S x2) a ha) 1) (Eqt M a 1)).

(; doc: A submonoid of a monoid `M` can be considered as a subsemigroup of that monoid. ;)
(; //LEAN:Submonoid.toSubsemigroup ;)
Submonoid__toSubsemigroup : (M : Set) -> (self : Elem (Submonoid M)) -> Elem (Subsemigroup M).

(; doc: `SubmonoidClass S M` says `S` is a type of subsets `s ≤ M` that contain `1` and are closed under `(*)` ;)
(; //LEAN:SubmonoidClass ;)
SubmonoidClass : (S : Set) -> (M : Set) -> Prop.

(; doc: The carrier of a subsemigroup. ;)
(; //LEAN:Subsemigroup.carrier ;)
Subsemigroup__carrier : (M : Set) -> (self : Elem (Subsemigroup M)) -> Elem (powerset M).

(; //LEAN:Subsemigroup.mk ;)
Subsemigroup__mk : (M : Set) -> (carrier : Elem (powerset M)) -> (mul_mem' : Proof (forall M (a => forall M (b => if (Membership__mem M (powerset M) carrier a) (if (Membership__mem M (powerset M) carrier b) (Membership__mem M (powerset M) carrier (times a b))))))) -> Elem (Subsemigroup M).

(; doc: All the elements of a type that satisfy a predicate.  `Subtype p`, usually written `{ x : α // p x }` or `{ x // p x }`, contains all elements `x : α` for which `p x` is true. Its constructor is a pair of the value and the proof that it satisfies the predicate. In run-time code, `{ x : α // p x }` is represented identically to `α`.  There is a coercion from `{ x : α // p x }` to `α`, so elements of a subtype may be used where the underlying type is expected.  Examples:  * `{ n : Nat // n % 2 = 0 }` is the type of even numbers.  * `{ xs : Array String // xs.size = 5 }` is the type of arrays with five `String`s.  * Given `xs : List α`, `List { x : α // x ∈ xs }` is the type of lists in which all elements are    contained in `xs`.  Conventions for notations in identifiers:   * The recommended spelling of `{ x // p x }` in identifiers is `subtype`. ;)
(; //LEAN:Subtype ;)
Subtype : (X : Set) -> (p : (Elem X -> Prop)) -> Set.

(; //LEAN:Subtype.coe_injective ;)
Subtype__coe_injective : (X : Set) -> (p : (Elem X -> Prop)) -> Proof (Function__Injective (Subtype X (x => p x)) X (a => Subtype__val X p a)).

(; //LEAN:Subtype.mk ;)
Subtype__mk : (X : Set) -> (p : (Elem X -> Prop)) -> (val : Elem X) -> (property : Proof (p val)) -> Elem (Subtype X (x => p x)).

(; doc: The value in the underlying type that satisfies the predicate. ;)
(; //LEAN:Subtype.val ;)
Subtype__val : (X : Set) -> (p : (Elem X -> Prop)) -> (self : Elem (Subtype X (x => p x))) -> Elem X.

(; doc: `a ∪ b` is the union of `a` and `b`.  Conventions for notations in identifiers:   * The recommended spelling of `∪` in identifiers is `union`. ;)
(; //LEAN:Union.union ;)
Union__union : (X : Set) -> (x : Elem X) -> (x1 : Elem X) -> Elem X.

(; //LEAN:ZeroHom.mk ;)
ZeroHom__mk : (M : Set) -> (N : Set) -> (toFun : (Elem M -> N)) -> (map_zero' : Proof (Eqt N (toFun 0) 0)) -> Elem (ZeroHom M N).

(; doc: `ZeroMemClass S M` says `S` is a type of subsets `s ≤ M`, such that `0 ∈ s` for all `s`. ;)
(; //LEAN:ZeroMemClass ;)
ZeroMemClass : (S : Set) -> (M : Set) -> Prop.

(; doc: By definition, if we have `ZeroMemClass S M`, we have `0 ∈ s` for all `s : S`. ;)
(; //LEAN:ZeroMemClass.zero_mem ;)
ZeroMemClass__zero_mem : (S : Set) -> (M : Set) -> (x : Proof (Zero M)) -> (x1 : Proof (SetLike S M)) -> (_ : Proof (ZeroMemClass S M)) -> (s : Elem S) -> Proof (Membership__mem M S s 0).

(; //LEAN:add_assoc ;)
add_assoc : (G : Set) -> (_ : Proof (AddSemigroup G)) -> (a : Elem G) -> (b : Elem G) -> (c : Elem G) -> Proof (Eqt G (plus (plus a b) c) (plus a (plus b c))).

(; //LEAN:add_neg_cancel_right ;)
add_neg_cancel_right : (G : Set) -> (_ : Proof (AddGroup G)) -> (a : Elem G) -> (b : Elem G) -> Proof (Eqt G (plus (plus a b) (Neg__neg G b)) a).

(; doc: Congruence in the function argument: if `a₁ = a₂` then `f a₁ = f a₂` for any (nondependent) function `f`. This is more powerful than it might look at first, because you can also use a lambda expression for `f` to prove that `<something containing a₁> = <something containing a₂>`. This function is used internally by tactics like `congr` and `simp` to apply equalities inside subterms.  For more information: [Equality](https://lean-lang.org/theorem_proving_in_lean4/quantifiers_and_equality.html#equality) ;)
(; //LEAN:congrArg ;)
congrArg : (X : Set) -> (Y : Set) -> (a1 : Elem X) -> (a2 : Elem X) -> (f : (Elem X -> Y)) -> (h : Proof (Eqt X a1 a2)) -> Proof (Eqt Y (f a1) (f a2)).

(; doc: The identity function. `id` takes an implicit argument `α : Sort u` (a type in any universe), and an argument `a : α`, and returns `a`.  Although this may look like a useless function, one application of the identity function is to explicitly put a type on an expression. If `e` has type `T`, and `T'` is definitionally equal to `T`, then `@id T' e` typechecks, and Lean knows that this expression has type `T'` rather than `T`. This can make a difference for typeclass inference, since `T` and `T'` may have different typeclass instances on them. `show T' from e` is sugar for an `@id T' e` expression. ;)
(; //LEAN:id ;)
id : (X : Set) -> (a : Elem X) -> Elem X.

(; //LEAN:inv_mul_cancel_left ;)
inv_mul_cancel_left : (G : Set) -> (_ : Proof (Group G)) -> (a : Elem G) -> (b : Elem G) -> Proof (Eqt G (times (Inv__inv G a) (times a b)) b).

(; //LEAN:inv_mul_cancel_right ;)
inv_mul_cancel_right : (G : Set) -> (_ : Proof (Group G)) -> (a : Elem G) -> (b : Elem G) -> Proof (Eqt G (times (times a (Inv__inv G b)) b) a).

(; doc: A version of `le_refl` where the argument is implicit ;)
(; //LEAN:le_rfl ;)
le_rfl : (X : Set) -> (_ : Proof (Preorder X)) -> (a : Elem X) -> Proof (Leq a a).

(; doc: **Alias** of the forward direction of `IsConcreteLE.le_iff`.  ---  The order corresponds to set inclusion. ;)
(; //LEAN:mem_of_le_of_mem ;)
mem_of_le_of_mem : (A : Set) -> (B : Set) -> (x : Proof (Membership B A)) -> (x1 : Proof (LE A)) -> (_ : Proof (IsConcreteLE A B)) -> (S : Elem A) -> (T : Elem A) -> (h : Proof (Leq S T)) -> (x2 : Elem B) -> (h1 : Proof (Membership__mem B A S x2)) -> Proof (Membership__mem B A T x2).

(; //LEAN:mul_assoc ;)
mul_assoc : (G : Set) -> (_ : Proof (Semigroup G)) -> (a : Elem G) -> (b : Elem G) -> (c : Elem G) -> Proof (Eqt G (times (times a b) c) (times a (times b c))).

(; //LEAN:mul_inv_cancel_right ;)
mul_inv_cancel_right : (G : Set) -> (_ : Proof (Group G)) -> (a : Elem G) -> (b : Elem G) -> Proof (Eqt G (times (times a b) (Inv__inv G b)) a).

(; //LEAN:neg_add_cancel_left ;)
neg_add_cancel_left : (G : Set) -> (_ : Proof (AddGroup G)) -> (a : Elem G) -> (b : Elem G) -> Proof (Eqt G (plus (Neg__neg G a) (plus a b)) b).

(; //LEAN:neg_add_cancel_right ;)
neg_add_cancel_right : (G : Set) -> (_ : Proof (AddGroup G)) -> (a : Elem G) -> (b : Elem G) -> Proof (Eqt G (plus (plus a (Neg__neg G b)) b) a).

(; //LEAN:nsmul_mem ;)
nsmul_mem : (M : Set) -> (A : Set) -> (_ : Proof (AddMonoid M)) -> (_ : Proof (AddSubmonoidClass A M)) -> (S : Elem A) -> (x2 : Elem M) -> (hx : Proof (Membership__mem M A S x2)) -> (n : Elem Nat) -> Proof (Membership__mem M A S (HSMul__hSMul Nat M M n x2)).

(; //LEAN:pow_mem ;)
pow_mem : (M : Set) -> (A : Set) -> (_ : Proof (Monoid M)) -> (_ : Proof (SubmonoidClass A M)) -> (S : Elem A) -> (x2 : Elem M) -> (hx : Proof (Membership__mem M A S x2)) -> (n : Elem Nat) -> Proof (Membership__mem M A S (pow x2 n)).

(; doc: The [axiom](https://lean-lang.org/doc/reference/4.36.0-rc1/find/?domain=Verso.Genre.Manual.section&name=axioms) of **propositional extensionality**. It asserts that if propositions `a` and `b` are logically equivalent (that is, if `a` can be proved from `b` and vice versa), then `a` and `b` are *equal*, meaning `a` can be replaced with `b` in all contexts.  The standard logical connectives provably respect propositional extensionality. However, an axiom is needed for higher order expressions like `P a` where `P : Prop → Prop` is unknown, as well as for equality. Propositional extensionality is intuitionistically valid. ;)
(; //LEAN:propext ;)
propext : (a : Prop) -> (b : Prop) -> (h : Proof (iff a b)) -> Proof (Eqt Prop a b).

(; doc: `rfl : a = a` is the unique constructor of the equality type. This is the same as `Eq.refl` except that it takes `a` implicitly instead of explicitly.  This is a more powerful theorem than it may appear at first, because although the statement of the theorem is `a = a`, Lean will allow anything that is definitionally equal to that type. So, for instance, `2 + 2 = 4` is proven in Lean by `rfl`, because both sides are the same up to definitional equality. ;)
(; //LEAN:rfl ;)
rfl : (X : Set) -> (a : Elem X) -> Proof (Eqt X a a).

